.SS "void sc_array_split (\fBsc_array_t\fP * array, \fBsc_array_t\fP * offsets, size_t num_types, \fBsc_array_type_t\fP type_fn, void * data)"

.PP
Compute the offsets of groups of enumerable types in an array\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarray\fP Array that is sorted in ascending order by type\&. If k indexes \fIarray\fP, then 0 <= \fItype_fn\fP (\fIarray\fP, k, \fIdata\fP) < \fInum_types\fP\&. 
.br
\fIoffsets\fP An initialized array of type size_t that is resized to \fInum_types\fP + 1 entries\&. The indices j of \fIarray\fP that contain objects of type k are \fIoffsets\fP[k] <= j < \fIoffsets\fP[k + 1]\&. If there are no objects of type k, then \fIoffsets\fP[k] = \fIoffset\fP[k + 1]\&. 
.br
\fInum_types\fP The number of possible types of objects in \fIarray\fP\&. 
.br
